# Compendium packs.
#
# A compiled pack is a live LevelDB, and Foundry writes to it whenever it opens one:
# CURRENT is rewritten and a fresh MANIFEST-* is spawned on open, and the .ldb files are
# rewritten on compaction. Committing that means every pull collides with whatever the
# local Foundry did last, which is exactly what happened. Ignoring only the churn is not
# an option either — CURRENT and MANIFEST-* are what make the store readable at all.
#
# So packs/_source is the committed form and the LevelDB is a build artefact:
# run "npm run build:packs" after cloning, and after any pull that touched
# packs/_source.
packs/*
!packs/_source
